###
### COMBINED FOLLOW/BLOCK SCENARIOS
###

### 1. Test blocking removes existing follows
### Profile1 currently follows Profile2 and Profile3
### Get Profile1's following list (should include Profile2, Profile3, Profile5)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile1}}/following

### 2. Block Profile2 - should remove the follow relationship
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/blocks/{{profile2}}
X-Profile-Id: {{profile1}}

### 3. Check Profile1's following list after blocking Profile2
### Expected: Profile3, Profile5 (Profile2 should be removed)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile1}}/following

### 4. Check Profile2's following list 
### Profile2 follows Profile3 and Profile4, but if Profile2 also followed Profile1, that would be removed
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile2}}/following

### 5. Create a bidirectional follow scenario and then block
### Profile3 follows Profile4, and Profile4 follows Profile3
### First verify they follow each other
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile3}}/following
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile4}}/following

### 6. Block in one direction - removes both follow relationships
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/blocks/{{profile3}}
X-Profile-Id: {{profile4}}

### 7. Verify both follow relationships are gone
### Profile3 no longer has Profile4 in following list
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile3}}/following

### Profile4 no longer has Profile3 in following list
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile4}}/following

###
### ERROR CASES FOR BLOCKS
###

### Try to block yourself (should fail with IllegalArgumentException)
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/blocks/{{profile1}}
X-Profile-Id: {{profile1}}

###
### ADVANCED SCENARIOS WITH USERS 7-10
###

### Test bidirectional block blocking
### Profile9 follows Profile10, Profile10 follows Profile9
### First verify the follows exist
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile9}}/following
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile10}}/following

### Profile9 blocks Profile10 - should remove both follow relationships
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/blocks/{{profile10}}
X-Profile-Id: {{profile9}}

### Verify the follows are gone
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile9}}/following
GET http://localhost:8081/api/follows/{{profile10}}/following
